  <diagram id="06-what-changes-as-the-level-rises" name="06-what-changes-as-the-level-rises" description="A grid with the four assurance levels across the top and three rows down the side. Signs it off: Level 1, you; Level 2, your team lead; Level 3, lead Official for Statistics; Level 4, lead Assurer, then the Analysis Senior Responsible Officer. Reviews it: Level 1, a colleague in your team; Level 2, someone with no hand in the work; Level 3, an assurer from outside the team; Level 4, a Lead Assurer, and external review. Ends with: Level 1, record stored with the output; Level 2, archived, and linked from the output; Level 3, published with its statement; Level 4, published, registered, revalidated annually.">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="680" pageHeight="530" math="0" shadow="0" background="#FFFFFF">
